{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator) requested implementation of task #5227: \"[stitch] cmd/logname: features implementation (srd053-logname R1.1-R2.2)\". This is a code generation task within the go-unix-utils project, which reimplements GNU coreutils in Go with differential testing against reference binaries. The specific deliverables are two new files: `cmd/logname/main.go` (the logname utility) and `cmd/logname/logname_test.go` (differential tests against glogname). Git operations are explicitly forbidden - the orchestrator handles git externally.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **logname utility**: Prints the login name from the system login record (getlogin(3) equivalent), NOT the effective UID\n   - **Differential testing**: Compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (glogname) byte-for-byte on stdout, stderr, and exit code\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: All cmd/ utilities must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main()\n   - **pkg/testutils**: Framework providing `BuildBinary`, `DiffTest` struct, and `RunDiffTests`\n   - **LC_ALL=C**: All differential tests must set this environment variable\n   - **Reference binary**: `glogname` from Homebrew GNU coreutils\n   - **Copyright header**: Every Go file must start with SPDX copyright header\n   - **Function size limit**: Hard 40-line limit per function\n   - **No git commands**: Git is managed externally by the orchestrator\n   - **Write-first strategy**: Write all source files before running build/test commands\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd053-logname.yaml** (READ)\n      - This is the SRD defining all requirements for the logname utility\n      - Key requirements