error, unknown flag error\n\n   - **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** (existing, provided inline)\n      - Contains `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` function\n      - Pattern: signal.Notify on buffered channel, goroutine exits 0 on SIGPIPE\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/** (existing, contract provided)\n      - `DiffTest` struct: `{ Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles }`\n      - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` \n      - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles cmd/ package\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only one read operation was performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Successfully identified and read the SRD file which was not included in the inline project context\n   - Identified the key implementation approach: use os.Getenv(\"LOGNAME\") as Go equivalent of getlogin(3) since Go doesn't wrap getlogin(3) directly without cgo\n   - No implementation has been done yet\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive task prompt from the cobbler orchestrator containing all project context, constitution, coding standards, task definition, requirements, constraints, and acceptance criteria for implementing cmd/logname\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/logname/main.go` implementing R1.1, R1.2, R2.1, R2.2\n   - Create `cmd/logname/logname_test.go` with differential tests\n   - Run `go build -o bin/logname ./cmd/logname/` to verify compilation (AC5)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/logname/ -count=1` to verify tests pass or skip gracefully (AC6)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd053-logname.yaml`) and was about to begin implementing the two source files. The task requires creating:\n   \n   **cmd/logname/main.go** - A simple utility that:\n   - Calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` first\n   - Checks for any arguments (extra operands or unknown flags → error + exit 1)\n   - Gets login name via system login record equivalent\n   - Prints login name + newline to stdout, exits 0\n   \n   **cmd/logname/logname_test.go** - Differential tests that:\n   - Build the binary with `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")`\n   - Look up `glogname` with `exec.LookPath`, skip if not found\n   - Define DiffTest cases with LC_ALL=C for: no-args invocation, extra operand, unknown flag\n   - Run via `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both files (`cmd/logname/main.go` and `cmd/logname/logname_test.go`) in full, then build and test. The task description states: \"Write all source files before running any build or test commands\" and the implementation strategy requires writing files in dependency order then building once. I should write main.go first, then logname_test.go, then run `go build` and `go test`.\n\n   Key implementation detail for main.go: In Go, the equivalent of C's `getlogin(3)` is typically `os.Getenv(\"LOGNAME\")` since Go doesn't provide a direct wrapper. The LOGNAME environment variable is set by the login process and represents the login identity. For flag/operand handling, since logname accepts no flags (except --help/--version which GNU adds), any argument should trigger an error. The simplest approach is to check `os.Args[1:]` manually rather than using a flag parser, matching how GNU logname behaves.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5227/7dca3a83-6a8a-499a-b5a4-dd16921e7384.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up th