{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016LWvJKG8c6ZMYCPFJcoVyV","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Findings\n\nI've thoroughly explored the repo patterns for implementing simple cmd/ utilities. Here are your answers:\n\n### 1. **Simple cmd/ utility main.go** (cmd/true/main.go)\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5227/cmd/true/main.go`\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// cmd/true exits with status 0, ignoring all arguments.\n// Implements srd013-true R1.1-R1.3, R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.2.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\nconst helpText = `Usage: true [ignored command line arguments]\n  or:  true OPTION\nExit with a status code indicating success.\n\n      --help     display this help and exit\n      --version  output version information and exit\n`\n\nconst versionText = `true (go-unix-utils) dev\n`\n\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n\tif len(os.Args) > 1 {\n\t\tswitch os.Args[1] {\n\t\tcase \"--help\":\n\t\t\tif _, err := fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\tcase \"--version\":\n\t\t\tif _, err := fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nThis is the simplest pattern: install SIGPIPE handler, check for --help/--version flags with argument handling, and exit appropriately.\n\n### 2. **Simple cmd/ utility test file** (cmd/basename/basename_test.go)\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5227/cmd/basename/basename_test.go`\n\nThe full file is shown above (132 lines). It demonstrates:\n- Building the binary with `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")`\n- Looking up a GNU reference binary (gbasename)\n- Creating DiffTest slices with various test cases\n- Using NormalizeFunc for output normalization (e.g., discarding stdout, regex replacements)\n- Calling `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)`\n\n### 3. **DiffTest struct definition** (from pkg/testutils/difftest.go)\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5227/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`\n\nThe struct fields (lines 46-55):\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string              // Subtest name (used with t.Run)\n\tArgs          []string            // Command-line arguments\n\tStdin         []byte              // stdin bytes (nil = EOF immediately)\n\tEnv           []string            // Environment variables (KEY=VALUE format)\n\tWorkDir       string              // Working directory (defaults to t.TempDir())\n\tExitCode      int                 // Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc      // Output normalizers applied in order\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte   // Files to check in WorkDir after execution\n}\n```\n\n### 4. **Copyright header format**\nThe consistent format used across all files:\n```\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n```\n\nFollowed by an optional blank line, then a package-level comment describing the utility (e.g., \"// cmd/true exits with status 0, ignoring all arguments.\") and specifications reference (e.g., \"// Implements srd013-true R1.1-R1.3, R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.2.\"), then `package main`.\n\n### 5. **cmd/logname/ directory status**\n**Status:** No cmd/logname/ directory exists yet. The cmd/ directory contains these utilities:\n- arch, basename, cat, dirname, du, false, head, hostid, hostname, ls, mktemp, nproc, seq, sponge, tee, true, uname, version\n\nYou're free to create cmd/logname/ following these established patterns."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7dca3a8